Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(predictions): AI price and demand outlook via Hugging
 Face

Adds GET /api/predictions: it summarises the caller's live listings and the
offers standing against them, asks the configured model for a fair price
range and demand level per listing, and returns strict JSON.

The token is read server-side from HF_TOKEN and never reaches the browser -
a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix here would let anyone loading the page spend against
the account. The frontend calls the backend, which holds the credential.

Model output is treated as untrusted: the response is parsed defensively
(fences stripped, JSON extracted), unknown product ids are dropped, prices
are coerced to positive numbers falling back to the listing price, and
demand is clamped to the known enum. Requests time out at 45s so a slow
completion cannot pin a serverless invocation open. Nothing here writes to
a product, offer or trade - it is advisory only, and the backend still
computes every amount that matters.

The dashboard panel fetches on demand rather than on mount, so rendering a
dashboard does not fire a model call.

